/**
 * Wave 4, family 7 (24 Sept 2026): entities named as strings on the pituitary, thymoma, salivary gland, cervical, vulvar
 * and vaginal pages (docs/CANCER-PAGES.md). Pituitary (5): the lineage-defined pituitary neuroendocrine tumour types of
 * the WHO 2022 endocrine classification, lactotroph, somatotroph, corticotroph, gonadotroph and thyrotroph. Thymoma (4):
 * types A and AB (one page, both GTF2I-mutant and indolent), B1, B2 and B3 (B1 with B2 on one page, B3 on its own),
 * and micronodular thymoma with lymphoid stroma. Salivary (2): acinic cell carcinoma and carcinoma ex pleomorphic
 * adenoma. Cervix (2): adenosquamous carcinoma and small cell neuroendocrine carcinoma. Vulva and vagina (3): Bartholin
 * gland carcinoma, vulvar melanoma and vaginal melanoma.
 *
 * Rule cases: the plurihormonal PIT1-lineage tumour stays a string on the parent (its literature in the sources read is
 * classification-level only); "thymoma with myasthenia gravis" and "stage III to IVA thymoma" are settings; the
 * thymoma type A and AB pages are combined because the WHO and ITMIG treat them as one indolent GTF2I-mutant group;
 * ciliary body and iris melanoma are site variants of uveal melanoma and stay strings. Every figure is quoted from the
 * paper or page named beside it. Registered in src/data/index.ts as cancersWave4EndocrineThoracicGynae.
 */
